From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: drawing -- an island paints its content with Direct2D

A XAML Island stayed blank. Now its window paints its content: on WM_PAINT the content is laid out to the window's size and drawn with Direct2D on the window's DC (a DC render target) -- the theme's background, then every visible element at its place, its children over it in order: a Panel's or Grid's Background (Grid's BorderBrush/BorderThickness/CornerRadius), a Border's Background and border (uniform thickness as a stroke inside, others as sides; rounded corners), a TextBlock's text in its Foreground or the theme's text colour. Layout invalidations and brush or text changes repaint the islands. The implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
